<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3183" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">appŏsĭtĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adp-</span></b> ),
			ōnis, f.
		appono, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a setting before.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: epularum, * <i><span class="en">Vulg. Eccli.
				30, 18</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cucurbitae,</span>”
				<i>the application of</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
					Aur. Acut. 3, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">criminis,</span>”
				<i>the imputation of crime</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Lampr. Com. 5</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
